<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Latin Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1204">1204</a>–<a href="/years/1261">1261</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Latin Empire of Constantinople, Empire of Romania, Constantinopolitan Empire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Latin Empire, officially the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, was a feudal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader state</a> founded by the leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> on lands captured from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, which lasted from 1204 to 1261. After the crusaders plundered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in April 1204, they chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor">Baldwin IX of Flanders</a> as emperor and divided Byzantine territory into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> states, with a Catholic emperor in place of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> one. Challenged by the Byzantine rump states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> and at constant war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, it declined steadily, and in 1261 the Nicene Empire recovered Constantinople under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a>. The last emperor, Baldwin II, went into exile.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>They set up a <b>Latin Empire</b>, and Byzantium never recovered its former strength.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Alexios Strategopoulos, a general of the Empire of Nicaea, led Nicaean forces to recapture Constantinople, held by the <b>Latin Empire</b> since the Fourth Crusade of 1204.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-25">25 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Genoa promised naval help against the <b>Latin Empire</b> of Constantinople and Venice in return for tax-free trade and access to the Black Sea.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-13">13 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Baldwin, Count of Flanders and a leader of the Fourth Crusade, was crowned in Hagia Sophia as the first emperor of the <b>Latin Empire</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-16">16 May in history</a></li></ul></section>
